      "description": "Human Resources Department Skip to Top Navigation Skip to Content Skip to Footer Eagle Connect Alumni Families APPLY GIVE Academics Admissions & Aid Online Programs Visit Close Search Are you looking for? Accepted Student Day Athletics Bookstore Calendar Canvas Commencement Course Offerings Directory Employment Housing Husson Supports Library Map Mental Health Resources Open House Registrar Student Accounts Student Employment Welcome Weekend Close Academics Programs View All Undergraduate Graduate/Professional Certificates Online Schools & Colleges College of Business College of Health and Professional Studies College of Science & Humanities New England School of Communications School of Online and Professional Studies Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Students Transfer Students Graduate Students International Initiatives Online Students Tuition & Costs Financial Aid Plan a Visit Apply Now Student Life Career Services Center for Student Success Dining Services Esports Husson Gear Residence Life Safety and Security Wellness Center About Accreditation 2023 NECHE Self-Study Consumer Information Distinguished Business Speaker Series Institute for Strategic Leadership and Workforce Development Partnerships Athletics Eagle Intranet Online Programs Apply Give Canvas Bookstore Nest Eagle Connect Calendar Map Contact Us Directory Library News Resources For Alumni Family Current Students Faculty & Staff Search Menu Human Resources Department Home Human Resources Human Resources Human Resources Employee Benefits Husson Supports Job Listings Non-Discrimination Policy Husson University Title IX Husson University has emerged as a leading institution for transforming students’ lives through the power of extraordinary teaching and experiential learning. Each of our employees is a valued contributor and works to help our students as they pursue their educational goals. The University offers a supportive and inclusive work environment and a competitive benefits package. If you would like to join our talented faculty and staff, explore our job listings. Husson University recruits and hires for all positions without regard to race or color, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, physical or mental disability, religion, age, ancestry or national origin, genetic information or other status protected by law. This policy applies to promotions, training, compensation and all other conditions related to employment. The University will make reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals in accordance with applicable law. Back to Top Husson University | 1 College Circle | Bangor, Maine | 04401-2929 207.941.7000 | admit@husson.edu | Facebook YouTube LinkedIn Instagram Flickr Careers Board of Trustees Safety & Security Non-Discrimination Policy Privacy Policy Accessibility Copyright © Husson University, 1997-2026"
